# Global generation of coherent sheaves with zero-dimensional support

A coherent sheaf on a proper scheme over a field is generated by global sections if its support
has dimension at most zero.  This is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AYT].

## Main results

The mathematics and the tag both live in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Cohomology.GlobalGeneration.ZeroDimensionalSupport`, on
`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_generatingSections_of_support_dim_le_zero`, which carries
`@[stacks 0AYT "(1), …"]` next to its `@[stacks 0B3J "global_generation"]`.  This module declares
nothing; it is the cross-reference from the Varieties chapter to that declaration.

## Implementation notes

The declaration proves the clause in a form more general than the clause states it: it assumes
`IsLocallyNoetherian X` where [Stacks, Tag 0AYT] assumes `X` proper over a field `k`.  Properness
over a field gives `IsLocallyNoetherian X` through
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian`, so clause (1) follows by
instantiation and nothing further is needed here.  Global generation is expressed by the
existence of a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` structure.

The tag 0AYT is written as an attribute on that declaration, which is where the repository's
convention puts a second tag (see `@[stacks 09DT "the absolute normal closure", stacks 0BMF
"absolute"]` in `StacksCore/FieldTheory/Normal/AlgClosed.lean`), and not as a standalone
`add_to_stacks` command: `add_to_stacks` warns and skips when the declaration it names already
carries the tag.

## References

